From 22d0f196e5bb15738ad91dd1faa6251bc7c00d7d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:21:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 42/49] Add the Bare welcome screen

A one time welcome on the first launch after install: the wordmark, a line about what the
browser is for, and a circle to start browsing, with the credit pinned to the bottom.

It is a view layered over ChromeTabbedActivity rather than an Activity of its own. That is
the whole reason it feels different to the first run experience it replaces: one window for
the entire sequence, with the browser already loaded underneath, so nothing opens twice.

The circle picks up from the system splash. Android draws the splash icon at 160dp in the
centre, so the circle starts there and travels down to its resting place while shrinking to
its own size. Timing it off the splash leaving, rather than off layout, is what makes it
continuous: layout happens while the splash is still on screen, so animating there ran the
travel behind it and the splash then dissolved into a circle that had already arrived.

Tapping it grows the circle past the furthest corner and fades out, revealing the browser.
Both parents disable child clipping, otherwise the circle is cut off at the edge of its slot
partway through. Haptic feedback goes through performHapticFeedback, which needs no
permission and respects the system setting.

Shown once, tracked in its own SharedPreferences file so it does not need a key registered
with the shared Chrome preferences. The flag is written when the welcome is shown rather
than when it is dismissed, so killing the app partway through does not bring it back.
